        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 117,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And again, I say unto you, I remember my servant Oliver Granger; behold, verily I say unto him that his name shall be had in sacred remembrance from generation to generation, forever and ever, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "IE the agent left by the Prophet to settle his affairs in Kirtland."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 117:12",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 117,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, let him contend earnestly for the redemption of the First Presidency of my Church, saith the Lord; and when he falls he shall rise again, for his sacrifice shall be more sacred unto me than his increase, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 157,
            "end": 166,
            "text": "TG Self-Sacrifice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Self-Sacrifice.",
            "prettyString": "TG Self-Sacrifice",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Self-Sacrifice",
                "entryId": "tg-self-sacrifice",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 117:13",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 117,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, let him come up hither speedily, unto the land of Zion; and in the due time he shall be made a merchant unto my name, saith the Lord, for the benefit of my people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 117:14",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 117,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore let no man despise my servant Oliver Granger, but let the blessings of my people be on him forever and ever.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
